speech:
Honorable Chair, distinguished delegates,

The delegation of China is honored to address this assembly on the vital intersection of healthcare and environmental sustainability. As our nation continues to advance, we recognize that the health of our people is intrinsically linked to the health of our environment.

Over the past decades, China has made significant strides in improving public health. Life expectancy has risen to over 78 years, and our healthcare system now provides coverage to approximately 90% of our population.However, we acknowledge that challenges remain, particularly in addressing the environmental factors that impact health.

Air pollution, for instance, has been a pressing concern. While measures have led to improvements, many cities still struggle to meet national and World Health Organization standards. :contentReference[oaicite:3]{index=3} Recognizing this, China has implemented comprehensive air pollution action plans and invested substantially in renewable energy, achieving our 2030 renewable energy target six years ahead of schedule. :contentReference[oaicite:4]{index=4}

In the healthcare sector, we are pioneering sustainable practices. Initiatives include the development of green hospitals and the integration of eco-friendly technologies. Notably, our efforts in medical waste management have led to a 39% increase in capacity since 2019, ensuring safer disposal and reduced environmental impact. :contentReference[oaicite:5]{index=5}

Furthermore, China is addressing the burden of chronic diseases, which account for a significant portion of mortality. Strategies encompass promoting healthier lifestyles and enhancing preventive care, aligning with our Healthy China 2030 initiative. :contentReference[oaicite:6]{index=6}

In conclusion, China reaffirms its commitment to fostering a healthcare system that not only heals but also sustains. We advocate for collaborative efforts to integrate environmental considerations into health policies, ensuring a healthier planet for future generations.

Thank you.

